From dd46392a5cb8e3437d7a9ef97df224e1ea9484a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BiasClear <noreply@biasclear.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 13:35:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] Explain eval: a planned call that never reached the
 model is not evidence (306 fix a)

report() counted a run as complete when planned rows were refused before
the model, so the injection and claim gates could pass with no injection
or rewrite ever sent, and pair parity on 1 of 5 samples.

- A run is complete only if every planned row reached the model, except
  an injection the fixtures expect to be refused at the door; that one
  makes the run incomplete if it reaches the model.
- New gate `exercised`, the counts in the results and failure flags, and
  a "planned / reached the model / accepted" line per part.
- The composer's pre-check codes (E_OUT_PLAIN_TEXT, E_OUT_HOW with no
  call) are refusals at the door, not validator rejections.

Regressions: all injections at the door; one pair sample at the door on
both sides; a held-out control refused by the pre-check (the 80% floor
still passes, only the new gate catches it); the expected-at-door case
both ways. Mutations of each condition fail a test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
